WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.712
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:02.712 --> 00:00:04.420
 When you're a smaller
competitor taking

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.790
on the big guys,
you have to come up

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:11.000
with fun, sometimes outrageous
ways of getting your brand

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.850
known, getting on
the front pages,

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.180
because you just don't
have the advertising spend

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:15.970
that the big guys.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.355
Try to do things that
make people smile,

00:00:18.355 --> 00:00:19.855
even if you make a
fool of yourself.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.970
Taking notes has been the
most important thing that I've

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.500
done in building businesses.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.310
I went to space and it was
an incredible day in my life.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:37.910
But I had a list
of 35 things that I

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.380
felt need to be improved upon.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.820
When I was floating,
I felt there

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.240
should be a handle on the
seats that go on the walls

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.190
that you could grab hold of.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.373
If I hadn't written some
of these things down.

00:00:48.373 --> 00:00:49.790
I would have
forgotten about them.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:52.250
I'd already forgotten about
them until I just read them now.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:53.208
By yourself a notebook.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.620
People who use the I-word
too much put people off,

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.090
and rightfully so.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:04.640
If you're in a team of
people, it's very important

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.390
that you talk about
us or we, or try

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:12.830
to avoid the I-word unless
it's absolutely necessary.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:17.410
And your business is likely
to excel as a result.

